# Information Density

## Clarity over density

- Compact but readable: visual density is fine, information overload is not.
  A page overloaded with information becomes unreadable for non-expert users
  (see `knowledge-base/ux/simple-ui.mdc`).

- Prefer compact cards.

- Prefer compact tables.

- Limit the information displayed in a Card so that the user can easily remember its position.

- Give sections breathing room with consistent spacing, without creating
  useless large empty areas.

## Information appears once

- Each fact must have a single visible location per screen: never show the
  same value more than once (header + card + list = unnecessary repetition).

- When a value is already displayed in the page header or a filter, do not
  repeat it inside the content.

- A count belongs only to the header of its own list/table and must not be
  duplicated in summary cards.

- Prefer a single compact summary that links to the detail view over
  duplicating the full data inline.

